\ The disk misbehaving (V4): a disk that stops answering, then answers again.
\ Its requests go to a queue the device was never given, so none completes.
7 block drop
data-disk @ disk d.vq @ constant real-vq
8 new-vq constant dead-vq
: deaf  ( -- )  dead-vq data-disk @ disk d.vq ! ;
: hear  ( -- )  real-vq data-disk @ disk d.vq ! ;
\ A read the disk never answers: -263, and no buffer claims the block.
deaf  9 ' block catch .  drop  hear
9 block c@ .
\ A write the disk never answers: -263, and the change waits to be written.
65 9 block c!  update
deaf  ' save-buffers catch .  hear
save-buffers  empty-buffers  9 block c@ .
\ And the system carries on.
2 3 + .
